Syntax: sew <slot> <race> <skein> <tier>
        sew refit <item> <slot>

Sew makes clothing or light armor from a skein of thread, sized to the race
you name.  It is the forge's mirror on the soft side, and it behaves the
same way: the skein's grade decides how much of the stats it carries come
through, and every missed stitch costs the piece a little of what it would
have been and the skein a little of what is left.

Hardness caps the tier here as everywhere.  Leather reaches light armor;
silk, however fine, never leaves clothing.

SEW REFIT <item> <slot> moves a soft piece onto a different part of the body,
the same work a smith does at an anvil for metal.  The body it was cut for
stays the same, the armor it offers is conserved across the move, growing
into a larger slot needs cloth for the difference, and shrinking leaves
clippings.

See also: WEAVE, SKEIN, TAILOR, FORGE
